---

The dictionary build in dictionaries/ downloads third-party data that is
distributed under its own licenses and is not covered by the license above.
Every input is pinned by URL and SHA-256 in dictionaries/sources.json together
with its SPDX license; dictionaries/policy.json says which licenses a package
may take. The inputs include:

* Universal Dependencies 2.19 - per treebank, mostly CC BY-SA 4.0, some
  non-commercial;
* UniMorph - per language, see the repositories at github.com/unimorph;
* Wiktionary through kaikki.org - CC BY-SA 4.0;
* national form-to-lemma dictionaries (for example SGJP and PoliMorf for
  Polish, BSD-2-Clause; OpenCorpora for Russian, CC BY-SA 3.0), each under the
  license recorded in sources.json.

Each dictionary package (udlex-dict-<iso>, wheel or archive) takes the
strictest license of its parts; packages named -nc are released under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for non-commercial use only. Every package carries the
treebank README and LICENSE, a NOTICE with the attribution of every input and
SOURCES.json with the license of each part.

When you redistribute a package, or a bundle built from these sources, you
redistribute that data as well: keep the corresponding notices.
